          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.107,
            0.844,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": "**2. What is the expression obtained by adding the 3 terms of any row, column, or diagonal?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.15,
            0.484,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** The expression obtained = 3 × m"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.171,
            0.842,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": "where m is the letter - number representing the number in the centre."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.201,
            0.462,
            0.219
          ],
          "content": "**3. Write the result obtained by**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.222,
            0.688,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Adding 1 to every term in the generalised form.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.242,
            0.667,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Doubling every term in the generalised form.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.265,
            0.169,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.286,
            0.196,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "(a)"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.302,
            0.629,
            0.408
          ],
          "content": "| m+ 4 | m-3 | m + 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| m-1 | m+ 1 | m+ 3 |\n| m | m+ 5 | m-2 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_27_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.409,
            0.196,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "(b)"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.428,
            0.648,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "| 2m+ 6 | 2m-8 | 2m+ 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2m-4 | 2m | 2m+ 4 |\n| 2m-2 | 2m+ 8 | 2m -6 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_27_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.555,
            0.636,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "**4. Create a magic square whose magic sum is 60. Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.593,
            0.617,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "| 23 | 16 | 21 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 18 | 20 | 22 |\n| 19 | 24 | 17 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_27_table_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.714,
            0.924,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": "**5. Is it possible to get a magic square by filling nine non-consecutive numbers?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.758,
            0.168,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.777,
            0.336,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "Yes, it is possible."
